# Source is LF everywhere: index normalized to LF and checked out as LF (box64 is a Linux-oriented
# codebase; the MSYS2/devkitPro toolchain is LF-native). This also fixes the phantom whole-tree-
# modified status on Windows (~2500 files were smudged to CRLF in the worktree by an earlier
# core.autocrlf setting while the index is LF). Files genuinely committed with CRLF upstream are
# left untouched — git skips conversion when the index blob already contains CRLF — so they don't
# become phantoms either. Real binaries (.exe/.dll/.nso/images) are auto-detected and never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows script/text formats keep CRLF (none in-tree today; pinned for future-proofing).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
